// D1640 — `fromCodePoints(e)` where `e` is not a bare name. The arm emitted its argument
// TWICE (once under `struct.get 0` for the backing, once under `struct.get 1` for the
// length), so it insisted on an `Ident` and refused a literal, a field, a call result and a
// slice alike. The argument is now spilled into one scratch local and read from there.
//
// THE ARGUMENT MUST STAY A NON-NAME. Binding it first (`const cps = [72, 105]`) takes the
// re-readable path that always ran, so a named-argument version greens every cell for the
// wrong reason.
//
// The spill slot is reserved module-wide off `moduleHasFcpSpill`, so `global_init` — which
// lays its frame out through `startFnDetectFrames`, a second code path — is the cell that
// says the reservation and the lowering agree.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@VALUE@@
fromCodePoints([72, 105])
// @@TYPE@@
string
// @@PROOF@@
print(v)
// @@TEST@@
v == "Hi"
// @@HIT@@
print(v)
// @@MISS@@
print("no")
// @@WANT@@
Hi
// @@VALUE2@@
fromCodePoints([72, 105, 33].slice(0, 3))
// @@TYPE2@@
string
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v)
// @@WANT2@@
Hi!
